BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Greetings from Davis: Write a Postcard Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T143000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53683260007656
DESCRIPTION:You’ve moooved into your apartment or res hall\, and classes
  have started. Let your friends and family back home know how you're doing
  the old-fashioned way — with a postcard! Drop by Shields Library and ou
 r Archives and Special Collections Department will provide everything you 
 need: a pen\, UC Davis Library postcard\, and postage.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, Lobby
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/greetings-from-davis-write-a-
 postcard-home-2026
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shields Library Mural Dedication
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T143000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54066200980920
DESCRIPTION:join us in celebrating our new library mural\, created by unde
 rgraduate students in the Mural Workshop (ART 171/CHI 171) in Spring 2026.
  Drawing on the Chicanx tradition of muralism\, the students' creative pro
 cess centered on community engagement\, collective storytelling\, and sens
 e of place. Vibrant imagery of students\, photos from the library's Univer
 sity Archives\, and an oak tree bearing the words “Saber es Poder” (
 “Knowledge is Power”) are among the elements that explore the library 
 as a space where preservation and empowerment meet. Learn more about the m
 ural.\n\nMeet some of the artists who created the mural and see footage of
  the making of this beautiful work of art. Light refreshments available wh
 ile they last. \nFree and open to all.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, Room 150 (east wing of the first floor)
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/mural-dedication
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Data Management Survival Skills
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53930518030098
DESCRIPTION:Working with and managing data is an essential skill for moder
 n researchers to conduct meaningful and impactful research. This workshop 
 will introduce you to better practices for file organization\, README’s\
 , flatfiles\, and data backups. No prior experience or expertise is requir
 ed or expected.\n\n \n\nRegister:\n\nZoom Registration\n\nIn-Person Regist
 ration
LOCATION:Walker Hall\, Gibeling Room or Zoom
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/data-management-survival-skil
 ls
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Letters and Science Authors Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T190000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54073373486698
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we celebrate faculty authors in the College of Lett
 ers and Science who have published a book in the past year. From scholarly
  monographs to creative writing\, book publication is a tremendous achieve
 ment. To all of our faculty authors\, we congratulate you! Wine and light 
 hors d’oeuvres will be served. Must be 21 or older to attend.\n\n \n\nBy
  invitation only—to receive an invitation\, contact the library's direct
 or of communications and external relations\, Jessica Nusbaum (jlnusbaum@u
 cdavis.edu).\n\n \n\nCo-hosted by the UC Davis Library\, the Jan Shrem and
  Maria Manetti Shrem Museum of Art\, and the College of Letters and Scienc
 e.\n\n \n\nVisit the Letters & Science Magazine Bookshelf to learn more ab
 out books published by faculty in the College.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, Courtyard
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/2026-letters-and-science-auth
 ors-celebration
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Copyright and Your Dissertation/Thesis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261016T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53941865896283
DESCRIPTION:The workshop will provide a general overview of U.S. Copyright
  Law\, with a focus on topics relevant to writing your thesis or dissertat
 ion. You’ll learn about copyright ownership of your work\, embargo optio
 ns\, and the UC Open Access Policies.\n\n \n\nRegister:\n\nZoom Registrati
 on\n\nIn-Person Registration
LOCATION:Walker Hall\, Gibeling Room or Zoom
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-copyright-and-your-d
 issertation
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:U.N. "Reboot the Earth" Hackathon
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261023
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53948926429434
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the United Nations\, the UC Davis Open Sou
 rce Program Office (OSPO)  and DataLab will host a "Reboot the Earth" hack
 athon. Reboot the Earth is a global initiative that addresses local climat
 e and environmental challenges through open source solutions. \n\nRepresen
 tatives of local agencies championing each challenge track will serve as s
 ubject matter experts\; students will also have access to mentors.\n\n \n\
 nWho: \n\nThe event is hosted by DataLab and the UC Davis Library\, and is
  open to students of all backgrounds and experience levels\, from any univ
 ersity or college. No prior hackathon experience is required—just curios
 ity and an eagerness to build something that matters. Participants are str
 ongly encouraged to form interdisciplinary teams and include peers from a 
 variety of majors. Each team may have a maximum of five people and has to 
 include at least one UC Davis student.\n\n \n\nWhy:\n\nContribute to solvi
 ng a problem in your community\n\nGet experience working on a cross-functi
 onal team\n\nRelease an open-source productThe winners are invited to UN O
 pen Source Week at United Nations Headquarters in New York! Travel expense
 s will be covered for the winning team. \n\nSchedule:\n\nKickoff Day (Octo
 ber 23)Wrap-up and Judging (October 24) Participation is required for at l
 east part of both days.\n\n \n\nLearn More:\n\nAt UC Santa Cruz's hackatho
 n in November 2025\, the winning team\, FireForm\, built an AI-powered voi
 ce-to-text tool that lets firefighters complete required documentation by 
 speaking naturally instead of typing. They continued developing it after t
 he event\, and it has since been certified as a United Nations Digital Pub
 lic Good. \n\n \n\nAt UC San Diego (May 2026)\, the winning team created F
 ireLink\, an SMS-based platform that delivers wildfire updates to resident
 s with no internet or smartphone required.\n\n \n\nThis Open Access Week e
 vent underlines the UC Davis Library’s commitment to open science.
LOCATION:Peter J. Shields Library at UC Davis\, 167
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/reboot-the-earth-hackathon-uc
 davis
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Open Access Publishing: How the UC Davis Library Can Sup
 port You
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53949236427976
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will explore the benefits of open access publish
 ing in scholarly journals. It will also provide an overview of institution
 al open access policies and funder mandates. Most importantly\, participan
 ts will learn about the open access publishing support available through t
 he University of California libraries consortium and UC Davis Library.\n\n
  \n\nRegister:\n\nZoom Registration
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-open-access-publishi
 ng
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
