BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scrapbook Aggie: Document Your Story with Archives and Special Col
 lections
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261028T143000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53683302378881
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join our Archives and Special Collections tea
 m on October 28 to document your own Aggie journey! \n\nWe’ll have scrap
 book supplies on hand (while they last) to get you started\, and you’re 
 also welcome to bring your own. Have you been collecting mementos or “ju
 nk” from your Aggie experience —tickets\, photos\, notes\, or receipts
 ? Bring them with you!\n\nOpen to the UC Davis community.\n \n\nQuestions?
  Contact Archives & Special Collections at SpecColl@ucdavis.edu.
LOCATION:Shields Library\, Lobby
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/scrapbook-aggie-document-your
 -story-with-archives-and-special-collections-2026
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Organize\, Cite\, Publish: Citation Management from Firs
 t Search to Final Draft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53949222829007
DESCRIPTION:Keep your sources\, notes\, PDFs\, and citations organized fro
 m your first search through your final draft. In this workshop\, we'll exp
 lore strategies for managing research throughout the literature review and
  publication process using citation management tools. Discover efficient w
 ays to import\, organize and tag sources\, annotate PDFs\, and generate ci
 tations and bibliographies. Come learn the tools and workflows that can sa
 ve you time—and make your thesis advisor a little envious.\n\n \n\nRegis
 ter:\n\nZoom Registration\n\nIn-Person Registration
LOCATION:Walker Hall\, Gibeling Room or Zoom
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-organize-cite-publis
 h-citation-management
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Mastering Your Literature Search: Techniques\, Tools and
  AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53949262091866
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is ideal for any student or researcher embarking
  on a literature search or review\, or anyone wanting to learn about emerg
 ing AI tools for literature searching. The session will cover (1) how to t
 ranslate your research question into a search strategy that will uncover t
 he scholarly literature you need\, (2) the library tools you will need for
  your searches\, and (3) an introduction to the AI tools designed for lite
 rature searching and how they can supplement your search strategy.\n\n \n\
 nRegister:\n\nZoom Registration\n\nIn-Person Registration
LOCATION:Walker Hall\, Gibeling Room or Zoom
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-mastering-your-liter
 ature-search
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: So you’re ready to publish your first scientific paper
 ?...
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53949248324551
DESCRIPTION:Publishing research in a scientific journal is a critical step
  in every researcher's journey. However\, it can be a very complex and int
 imidating landscape when doing it for the first time. This workshop will p
 rovide an introduction to major parts of the process including\, an overvi
 ew of the scientific publishing landscape\, selecting a journal\, working 
 with collaborators\, and more! This workshop is aimed at all STEM-aligned 
 fields and all experience levels\, but beginners are especially welcome.\n
 \n \n\nRegister:\n\nZoom Registration\n\nIn-Person Registration
LOCATION:Walker Hall\, Gibeling Room or Zoom
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-publish-your-first-s
 cientific-paper
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: AI Research Tools
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T130000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53949273778774
DESCRIPTION:The goal of this workshop is for attendees to build an awarene
 ss of the various AI tools available to them at different stages of the re
 search process. Workshop attendees will receive a brief introduction to so
 me of the different AI tools that will support them with literature search
 ing\, reading scholarly articles\, coding and programming\, and writing. N
 o prerequisite knowledge or experience is necessary to attend this worksho
 p.\n\n \n\nRegister:\n\nZoom Registration\n\nIn-Person Registration
LOCATION:Walker Hall\, Gibeling Room or Zoom
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/workshop-artificial-intellige
 nce-research-tools
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
